# Build context exclusions for the Docker image.
#
# # Why this file is not optional
#
# `target/` in this workspace is large — a debug build of 18 crates — and the Docker build context is
# copied to the daemon before anything runs. Without this file, `docker build` ships gigabytes the
# Dockerfile then ignores, and the build appears to hang with no error.
#
# # And it is a correctness file, not only a speed one
#
# `contracts/lib/` holds a Foundry dependency that CI fetches rather than commits, and `client/`
# holds a Tauri tree whose own `target/` is separate. Copying either into the image would put
# build artifacts of a different toolchain inside a Rust build stage.
#
# The entries mirror `.gitignore` deliberately: what is not in the repository should not be in the
# image, and having the two lists agree is easier to check than having one derive from the other.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
target/
**/target/
*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- runtime state
nau-data/
**/nau-data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.jsonl
*.snapshot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# A credential must never be baked into a layer: layers are readable by anyone who can pull the
# image, and `docker history` shows the commands even when the file is later deleted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
secrets.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- not needed to build the node
client/
DSH插件/
docs/
integrations/
sdks/
.github/
.work/
coverage/
*.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain artifacts
contracts/lib/
contracts/cache/
contracts/out/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editors and VCS
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
